---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Run Veasel Code from source"
  description="Set up the V backend, choose a model provider, and open the Veasel Code terminal client."
>
  <section class="doc-page page-grid">
    <p class="kicker">FIELD GUIDE / FIRST SESSION</p>
    <h1>
      From clone to
      <br />
      <em>conversation.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Veasel Code is under active development and currently runs from source.
      This guide starts the local V server and connects the terminal client to a
      provider you choose.
    </p>
    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>What you need</h2>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          The V compiler revision recorded in the repository’s{" "}
          <code>.v-version</code>.
        </li>
        <li>SQLite development headers and library for the V SQLite module.</li>
        <li>Bun 1.3.14 or newer to build and run the OpenTUI client.</li>
        <li>An API key for OpenAI-compatible, Anthropic, or Gemini models.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The backend itself is V and does not need Bun. V builds the OpenTUI
        terminal client on first use.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Start the V server</h2>
      <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel
cd veasel
export VEASEL_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic
export VEASEL_MODEL=your-model-name
export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-api-key
v run . serve</code></pre>
      <p>
        The server listens on <code>127.0.0.1:4097</code>. Keep your key in the
        server environment. Veasel does not send it to the terminal client or
        return it from the API.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Open a session</h2>
      <pre><code># In another terminal, from the repository
v run . tui</code></pre>
      <p>
        Create a session by selecting an existing workspace directory. Ask a
        question and the configured provider will answer. Messages and session
        events are persisted locally in SQLite.
      </p>
    </div>
    <aside class="callout">
      <strong>Know the current boundary.</strong> Veasel stores conversation
      history locally, but sends prompts to your configured model provider. The
      current build cannot read repository files, apply edits, or execute
      commands. See the{" "}
      <a href={`${basePath}/docs/security/`}>security notes</a>
      before using sensitive source code.
    </aside>
    <p class="doc-next">
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/providers/`}>
        Configure another provider <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/`}>
        Back to the field guide <span aria-hidden="true">↑</span>
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
